{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011DEkXrCsjEXPYNF6Jay68d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\tEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n5\t\n6\t## Title\n7\tOntoCoDec: Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n8\t(D015: \"Near-Complete\" dropped — DocRED residual DR=10.21% (Qwen) 不算 near-complete。论文贡献是方法，不是特定消除率。SciERC 0.93% 和 DocRED 2.55% (Llama) 可在正文中描述为 near-complete，但 title 不宜 overclaim。)\n9\t\n10\t## Core Insight\n11\tLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n12\t\n13\t**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n14\t- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n15\t- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n16\t- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n17\t- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n18\t\n19\t## Core Claims\n20\t\n21\t### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\n22\tLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n23\t\n24\t**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n25\t\n26\t**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n27\t\n28\t**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n29\t\n30\t### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\n31\tSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n32\t- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n33\t- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n34\t- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n35\t\n36\t**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n37\t\n38\t### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\n39\tOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n40\t1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n41\t2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n42\t\n43\tThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n44\t\n45\tThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n46\t\n47\t**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\n48\tWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n49\t\n50\t**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n51\t- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n52\t- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n53\t- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n54\t- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n55\t\n56\t**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n57\t\n58\t**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n59\t\n60\t**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n61\t- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n62\t- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n63\t- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n64\t\n65\t### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n66\t- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n67\t- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n68\t\n69\t**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n70\t\n71\t⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n72\t\n73\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n74\t\n75\t### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n76\t**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n77\t\n78\t### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n79\t**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n80\t\n81\tPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n82\t\n83\t**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n84\t1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n85\t2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n86\t3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n87\t4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n88\t\n89\t数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n90\t\n91\t**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n92\t5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n93\t6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n94\t7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n95\t\n96\t### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n97\t**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n98\t\n99\t### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n100\t**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n101\t\n102\t**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n103\t\n104\t### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n105\t**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE (D016 bootstrap verified). Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n106\t- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS\n107\t- DocRED: DR 26.07%→2.55% (↓90.2%), R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013, significant), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022, modest decline)\n108\t- Parse failures: unconstrained 68 vs full_s1 91 (6.8% vs 9.1%)\n109\t\n110\t**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n111\t- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n112\t- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n113\t- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n114\t- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n115\t- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n116\t- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n117\t\n118\t### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n119\t**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Bootstrap CI (10000×, D012 Qwen + D016 Llama, all registry-aligned)**:\n120\t\n121\t**Qwen3-8B**: SciERC R-F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58, NS), E-F1 -0.03pp (NS). DocRED R-F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001), E-F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001).\n122\t**Llama-3.1-8B**: SciERC R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS. DocRED R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022).\n123\t\n124\t**Cross-model pattern**: DocRED R-F1 显著提升（两个模型）。E-F1 model-dependent（Qwen +1.23pp, Llama -0.64pp）。\n125\t- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n126\t- Frame as: \"On DocRED, R-F1 gains are significant for both models. Entity F1 impact is model-dependent.\"\n127\t- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告。\n128\t\n129\t### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n130\t**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n131\t\n132\t**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n133\t- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n134\t- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n135\t- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n136\t\n137\t**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n138\t\n139\t**论证层次**：\n140\t1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n141\t2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n142\t3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n143\t4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n144\t\n145\t**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n146\t\n147\t**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n148\t\n149\t**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n150\t\n151\t### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n152\t**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n153\t\n154\t## Paper Structure (Draft)\n155\t1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n156\t2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n157\t3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n158\t4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n159\t5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n160\t6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n161\t7. Conclusion\n162\t\n163\t## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n164\t\n165\t**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n166\t- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n167\t- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n168\t- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n169\t- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n170\t- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n171\t\n172\t**Claim with caution**:\n173\t- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n174\t- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n175\t- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n176\t- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n177\t\n178\t**Do NOT claim**:\n179\t- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n180\t- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n181\t- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n182\t- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n183\t- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n184\t- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n185\t- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n186\t\n187\t## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n188\t\n189\t1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n190\t2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n191\t3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n192\t4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n193\t5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n194\t\n195\t## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n196\t\n197\t- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n198\t- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n199\t- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED 2 组实验 ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc baseline ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n200\t- **May 14-15**: D014 tightness claim 修订 + §5 cross-model subsection + abstract/conclusion 修正 (Agent 执行中)\n201\t- **May 15-17**: 全文校对 + Discussion 整合 + 最终数字确认\n202\t- **May 19**: 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n203\t- **May 19-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n204\t\n205\t**当前瓶颈**: 无技术 blocker。等 Reviewer 跨文件一致性审查 + 编译验证后即可 submit_paper_to_review。\n206\t\n207\t## Status\n208\t- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n209\t- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n210\t- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n211\t- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n212\t- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n213\t- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n214\t- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n215\t- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n216\t- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n217\t- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n218\t- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n219\t- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n220\t- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n221\t- D014 tightness revision: ✅ Complete (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n222\t- Llama bootstrap CI (D016): ✅ Fixed + verified (registry-aligned ≤0.05pp, all p-values in paper)\n223\t- Paper compilation: ✅ 8 pages正文 + appendix\n224\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7520a298-8466-4fc2-9ef4-158ddc28c35f","uuid":"caa3f615-9fe4-46bb-aaf8-4b294b795d1f","timestamp":"2026-05-16T18:00:25.930Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T173022/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n\n## Target Venue\nEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n\n## Title\nOntoCoDec: Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n(D015: \"Near-Complete\" dropped — DocRED residual DR=10.21% (Qwen) 不算 near-complete。论文贡献是方法，不是特定消除率。SciERC 0.93% 和 DocRED 2.55% (Llama) 可在正文中描述为 near-complete，但 title 不宜 overclaim。)\n\n## Core Insight\nLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n\n**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\nLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n\n**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n\n**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n\n**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n\n### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\nSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n\n**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n\n### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\nOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n\nThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n\nThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n\n**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\nWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n\n**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n\n**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n\n**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n\n**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n\n**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n\n⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n\n### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n\nPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n\n**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n\n数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n\n**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n\n### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n\n### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n\n**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n\n### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE (D016 bootstrap verified). Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS\n- DocRED: DR 26.07%→2.55% (↓90.2%), R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013, significant), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022, modest decline)\n- Parse failures: unconstrained 68 vs full_s1 91 (6.8% vs 9.1%)\n\n**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n\n### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Bootstrap CI (10000×, D012 Qwen + D016 Llama, all registry-aligned)**:\n\n**Qwen3-8B**: SciERC R-F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58, NS), E-F1 -0.03pp (NS). DocRED R-F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001), E-F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001).\n**Llama-3.1-8B**: SciERC R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS. DocRED R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022).\n\n**Cross-model pattern**: DocRED R-F1 显著提升（两个模型）。E-F1 model-dependent（Qwen +1.23pp, Llama -0.64pp）。\n- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n- Frame as: \"On DocRED, R-F1 gains are significant for both models. Entity F1 impact is model-dependent.\"\n- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告。\n\n### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n\n**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n\n**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n\n**论证层次**：\n1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n\n**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n\n**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n\n**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n\n### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (Draft)\n1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n7. Conclusion\n\n## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n\n**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n\n**Claim with caution**:\n- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n\n**Do NOT claim**:\n- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n\n## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n\n1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n\n## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n\n- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED 2 组实验 ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc baseline ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n- **May 14-15**: D014 tightness claim 修订 + §5 cross-model subsection + abstract/conclusion 修正 (Agent 执行中)\n- **May 15-17**: 全文校对 + Discussion 整合 + 最终数字确认\n- **May 19**: 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n- **May 19-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n\n**当前瓶颈**: 无技术 blocker。等 Reviewer 跨文件一致性审查 + 编译验证后即可 submit_paper_to_review。\n\n## Status\n- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n- D014 tightness revision: ✅ Complete (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n- Llama bootstrap CI (D016): ✅ Fixed + verified (registry-aligned ≤0.05pp, all p-values in paper)\n- Paper compilation: ✅ 8 pages正文 + appendix\n","numLines":224,"startLine":1,"totalLines":224}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YZsqLehxdQLxZf6oNQedib","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Zero-shot Qwen3-8B 在 SciERC 上的 ontology constraint violation baseline\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"total_triples\": 1680,\n7\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.128,\n8\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.005,\n9\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.018,\n10\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n11\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.295,\n12\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.076,\n13\t      \"per_relation_dr_variance\": 0.008,\n14\t      \"max_per_relation_dr\": 0.31,\n15\t      \"min_per_relation_dr\": 0.04\n16\t    },\n17\t    \"tables\": [\n18\t      \"Table 1: Per-relation DR distribution — relatively flat, max/min ratio ~8× (not 55× as needed for tightness argument)\"\n19\t    ],\n20\t    \"figures\": [],\n21\t    \"analysis\": \"审稿人攻击线：\\\"The violation rates are moderate and relatively uniform — this is \\nsimply what happens when you ask an LLM to generate structured output without fine-tuning.\\nThe 'violation landscape' contribution reduces to measuring a known phenomenon.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档位下，DR 约 12.8%——仍属 non-trivial 但低于 15% 的 \\\"impressive\\\" 门槛。\\n关键问题：per-relation DR variance 较低（σ²=0.008），violations 分布相对均匀，\\n削弱了 \\\"constraint tightness drives concentration\\\" 的核心 insight。\\n审稿人会说：\\\"12.8% violation rate across 7 relations is expected for any structured \\ngeneration task — this is not a surprising finding worthy of a dedicated landscape study.\\\"\\n最高单关系 DR 仅 31%（非 42%），不够极端来论证 per-relation guarantee 的必要性。\\n\"\n22\t  },\n23\t  {\n24\t    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n25\t    \"description\": \"Schema-informed prompt 对 SciERC violations 的消除效果\",\n26\t    \"results\": {\n27\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.041,\n28\t      \"total_triples\": 1640,\n29\t      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction\": -0.68,\n30\t      \"per_relation_evaluate_for_delta\": -0.02,\n31\t      \"per_relation_feature_of_delta\": -0.24,\n32\t      \"per_relation_all_improved\": true,\n33\t      \"mcnemar_significant\": true\n34\t    },\n35\t    \"tables\": [],\n36\t    \"figures\": [],\n37\t    \"analysis\": \"如果 prompt 足够好且无 regression，整个 \\\"prompt insufficiency\\\" claim 被削弱。\\n审稿人会追问：\\\"Why not iterate on prompt engineering (few-shot, chain-of-thought) \\nbefore building a complex decoding system?\\\" OntoCoDec 变成 over-engineering 的例证。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档：schema-informed prompt 将 DR 从 12.8% 降到 4.1%（↓68%），且所有关系类型均有改善\\n（Evaluate-for 也下降 2pp 而非实际的 +5.8pp regression）。审稿人论证：\\n\\\"A well-crafted prompt already achieves 68% reduction with zero engineering effort. \\nThe remaining 4.1% is close to noise level for zero-shot extraction. The cost-benefit \\nof building a compiler + runtime constraint system for the last 4pp is questionable.\\\"\\n没有 per-relation regression = 丢失了 \\\"prompt unreliable at per-relation level\\\" 这个关键论据。\\n\"\n38\t  },\n39\t  {\n40\t    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n41\t    \"description\": \"DocRED 96-relation ontology 的 zero-shot violation baseline\",\n42\t    \"results\": {\n43\t      \"total_triples\": 16200,\n44\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.155,\n45\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.068,\n46\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.295,\n47\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n48\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.958\n49\t    },\n50\t    \"tables\": [\n51\t      \"Table 2: Cross-dataset comparison — DR rates within 3pp, undermining urgency narrative\"\n52\t    ],\n53\t    \"figures\": [],\n54\t    \"analysis\": \"RV=29.5% 被审稿人视为 grammar 层的 \\\"free lunch\\\"——单层 CFG constraint 就能消除的 trivial violation，\\n不需要复杂的 semantic layer。\\\"Most of the violations (29.5% RV + 6.8% ET = 36.3%) are \\ntrivially fixable by grammar alone; only 15.5% require semantic reasoning.\\\"\\n\\n\\nDR=15.5% 与 SciERC 12.8% 接近（比值 1.2×）——审稿人论证：\\n\\\"Violation rates are comparable across a 7-relation and 96-relation ontology (15.5% vs 12.8%). \\nThis directly contradicts any claim about ontology complexity driving violations — \\nthe rates are essentially the same regardless of schema size.\\\"\\n这个数据点本应支持 \\\"tightness not size\\\" 的 insight，但在 worst 档位下被反过来读：\\n既然 rate 不随 size 变化，问题规模本身就是 bounded（不像论文暗示的那样严峻）。\\n\"\n55\t  },\n56\t  {\n57\t    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n58\t    \"description\": \"Schema-informed prompt 在 DocRED 上的效果\",\n59\t    \"results\": {\n60\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.098,\n61\t      \"dr_reduction_vs_minimal\": -0.37,\n62\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n63\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.19\n64\t    },\n65\t    \"tables\": [],\n66\t    \"figures\": [],\n67\t    \"analysis\": \"审稿人构建 \\\"diminishing returns\\\" 叙事：Prompt ↓37% (free) → FT ↓95% (standard) → \\nConstrained decoding covers the last 2% at the cost of CF↑10× and latency overhead.\\n\\\"The method lives in a narrow utility window that disappears with standard fine-tuning.\\\"\\n\\n\\nDR 降到 9.8%（↓37%）——比 SciERC 的 ↓68% 弱，但审稿人不关注这个 gap：\\n\\\"Even with a simple schema-informed prompt, DR drops to under 10%. Combined with \\nthe fact that fine-tuning reduces DR to <2%, the remaining window where constrained \\ndecoding adds value is extremely narrow (the 2-10% gap that prompt can't close but \\nFT can).\\\" 这直接喂 \\\"FT makes the method unnecessary\\\" 攻击线。\\n\"\n68\t  },\n69\t  {\n70\t    \"name\": \"SciERC unconstrained baseline\",\n71\t    \"description\": \"SciERC Phase 2 unconstrained 重跑（checker v2 对齐）\",\n72\t    \"results\": {\n73\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.128,\n74\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.018,\n75\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.005,\n76\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n77\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.295,\n78\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.076,\n79\t      \"total_triples\": 1680\n80\t    },\n81\t    \"tables\": [],\n82\t    \"figures\": [],\n83\t    \"analysis\": \"低 F1 baseline 是 C8 攻击面的核心弹药。Worst 档审稿人不会接受 \\\"F1 is control variable\\\"\\n的论证——他们会说 \\\"if the base extraction is this poor, constraint enforcement \\nis premature optimization on garbage.\\\"\\n\\n\\n与 P001 一致（同一模型同一数据集），作为 Phase 2 ablation 的对照基线。\\nWorst 档位下 baseline F1 已经很低（R-F1 7.6%），审稿人会质疑：\\n\\\"Evaluating constraint methods on a setting with 7.6% relation F1 is meaningless — \\nthe model barely extracts anything correctly. Any constraint enforcement on \\nnear-random outputs is academic exercise, not useful research.\\\"\\n\"\n84\t  },\n85\t  {\n86\t    \"name\": \"SciERC grammar-only\",\n87\t    \"description\": \"仅 grammar 层（CFG）对 SciERC 的约束效果\",\n88\t    \"results\": {\n89\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n90\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0,\n91\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.125,\n92\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n93\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.294,\n94\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.075\n95\t    },\n96\t    \"tables\": [],\n97\t    \"figures\": [],\n98\t    \"analysis\": \"Grammar 层的效果完全可预期且 trivial——这是 worst 档审稿人最强的 novelty 攻击弹药。\\n\\\"Layer 1 is off-the-shelf XGrammar. Layer 2 is a type checker. The paper's contribution \\nis connecting them with bitwise AND — this is systems integration, not research.\\\"\\n\\n\\nGrammar 层消除 ET/RV（trivial CFG-expressible constraints），但 DR 仅从 12.8%→12.5%\\n（↓2.3%，negligible）。F1 微降 0.1pp。审稿人的读法：\\n\\\"The grammar layer does exactly what XGrammar was designed to do — enforce vocabulary \\nconstraints. This is a direct application of existing technology (XGrammar, Zheng et al. 2024) \\nwith zero methodological novelty. The authors simply configured XGrammar for their JSON schema.\\\"\\n这直接喂 \\\"engineering contribution\\\" 的 novelty 攻击。\\n\"\n99\t  },\n100\t  {\n101\t    \"name\": \"SciERC semantic-only\",\n102\t    \"description\": \"仅 semantic 层（logit masking）对 SciERC 的约束效果\",\n103\t    \"results\": {\n104\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.088,\n105\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.005,\n106\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.018,\n107\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.035,\n108\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.292,\n109\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.073\n110\t    },\n111\t    \"tables\": [],\n112\t    \"figures\": [],\n113\t    \"analysis\": \"Semantic-only 的 CF 引入是最致命的数据点：它证明 semantic 层 IS the source of CF，\\n且没有 grammar 层时效果很差。审稿人会说 \\\"the semantic layer is both the cause of \\nthe new problem (CF) and insufficient to solve the original problem (DR) without grammar.\\\"\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only 将 DR 从 12.8%→8.8%（↓31%），但引入 CF=3.5%（从 0.1% 暴涨 35×）。\\nF1 下降 0.3pp。审稿人攻击：\\\"The semantic layer alone achieves only 31% DR reduction \\nwhile introducing 35× more cross-field inconsistencies. This is a net negative — \\nthe method creates more problems than it solves.\\\"\\n且 ET/RV 无法处理（因为没有 grammar 层），暴露 enabling dependency 但被读为 \\\"单层无法独立工作 = 设计耦合\\\"。\\n\"\n114\t  },\n115\t  {\n116\t    \"name\": \"SciERC full S1\",\n117\t    \"description\": \"Grammar+Semantic 双层 single-pass decoding 对 SciERC 的完整效果\",\n118\t    \"results\": {\n119\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.025,\n120\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n121\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0,\n122\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.142,\n123\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.289,\n124\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.071,\n125\t      \"fallback_rate\": 0.41\n126\t    },\n127\t    \"tables\": [\n128\t      \"Table 3: Violation trade-off — DR↓10.3pp vs CF↑14.1pp, net violation increase\"\n129\t    ],\n130\t    \"figures\": [],\n131\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档位的核心数据：方法引入的 CF 大于它消除的 DR。\\ntotal_violation_before = 12.8% + 1.8% + 0.5% + 0.1% = 15.2%\\ntotal_violation_after = 2.5% + 0% + 0% + 14.2% = 16.7%\\n审稿人可以合法地声称 \\\"the method makes things worse on aggregate.\\\"\\n即使论证 DR > CF in severity，这个 framing 对 EMNLP reviewer 极具说服力。\\n\\n\\nDR 从 12.8%→2.5%（↓80%），但 CF 从 0.1%→14.2%（↑142×）。\\nR-F1 下降 0.5pp（p=0.03, statistically significant）。\\n审稿人的核心攻击：\\n\\\"The method reduces DR by 10.3pp but introduces CF at 14.2pp — a net INCREASE \\nin total violation load. The authors are trading known, measurable violations \\n(DR) for harder-to-detect inconsistencies (CF). This is not improvement, \\nit's problem displacement.\\\"\\nFallback rate 41% 意味着近半数 token 位置 semantic mask 失效——方法在很多时刻\\n实质上只有 grammar-only 在工作。DR 残余 2.5%（非 near-complete）进一步削弱 claim。\\n\"\n132\t  },\n133\t  {\n134\t    \"name\": \"SciERC full S2 (ablation)\",\n135\t    \"description\": \"Two-pass S2 策略作为 CF mitigation 的尝试\",\n136\t    \"results\": {\n137\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.028,\n138\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.128,\n139\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.285,\n140\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.068,\n141\t      \"total_entities\": 2180\n142\t    },\n143\t    \"tables\": [],\n144\t    \"figures\": [],\n145\t    \"analysis\": \"S2 在所有指标上都不如 S1 或仅 marginal 改善——审稿人会说 \\\"the authors tried to fix CF \\nwith a two-pass approach and failed. This confirms CF is a fundamental limitation \\nof the approach, not an engineering issue that can be resolved.\\\"\\n\\n\\nS2 DR=2.8%（比 S1 的 2.5% 更差），CF=12.8%（比 S1 的 14.2% 稍好但仍然极高）。\\nR-F1 6.8%（比 S1 的 7.1% 更差 0.3pp）。Entity 数量从 2474 降到 2180（↓12%）——\\nS2 pass-1 的 entity extraction 更保守但不更准确。\\n审稿人：\\\"The two-pass variant slightly reduces CF (14.2%→12.8%) but at the cost of \\nworse F1 and higher DR. The proposed architectural solution to CF does not work.\\\"\\nS2 无法作为 CF mitigation 的证据，也无法作为 interesting architectural contribution。\\n\"\n146\t  },\n147\t  {\n148\t    \"name\": \"DocRED unconstrained baseline\",\n149\t    \"description\": \"DocRED Phase 2 unconstrained（checker v2, all_set F1）\",\n150\t    \"results\": {\n151\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.155,\n152\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.295,\n153\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.068,\n154\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n155\t      \"entity_f1\": 56.8,\n156\t      \"relation_f1\": 7.2,\n157\t      \"total_triples\": 17100,\n158\t      \"unrecognized_relations\": 5050\n159\t    },\n160\t    \"tables\": [],\n161\t    \"figures\": [],\n162\t    \"analysis\": \"High RV% 在 worst 档被解读为 \\\"大部分 contribution 来自 off-the-shelf grammar constraint\\\"，\\n留给 semantic 层的独有贡献空间只有 15.5pp DR。\\n\\n\\nDocRED baseline 的 RV=29.5% 和 ET=6.8% 是 grammar 层的 \\\"easy wins\\\"——\\n审稿人会计算：\\\"36.3% of violations are trivially fixable by vocabulary constraint \\n(XGrammar direct application), only 15.5% require the novel semantic layer.\\\"\\nE-F1=56.8% 比 SciERC 高很多，因为 DocRED entity recognition 相对简单\\n（named entities vs scientific terms）。R-F1=7.2% 仍然很低。\\n\"\n163\t  },\n164\t  {\n165\t    \"name\": \"DocRED grammar-only\",\n166\t    \"description\": \"DocRED 仅 grammar 层约束\",\n167\t    \"results\": {\n168\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n169\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n170\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.25,\n171\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n172\t      \"entity_f1\": 58.5,\n173\t      \"relation_f1\": 7.9\n174\t    },\n175\t    \"tables\": [\n176\t      \"Table 4: Grammar-only achieves ALL of the F1 improvement; semantic layer contributes zero F1 gain\"\n177\t    ],\n178\t    \"figures\": [],\n179\t    \"analysis\": \"\\\"Grammar layer = all F1 gain. Semantic layer = DR↓ + CF↑ + 0 F1 impact.\\\" \\n这是 worst 档审稿人最简洁有力的论证——semantic 层的 contribution 是 DR→CF 的 trade-off，\\n而非 F1 improvement。整个 semantic 层可以被 post-hoc filter 替代且更简单。\\n\\n\\nGrammar-only 消除 RV 和 ET（36.3pp violations gone），E-F1 提升 1.7pp（从 OOV relation \\n不再作为 FP 计入），R-F1 提升 0.7pp。DR 从 15.5%→25.0%——注意 DR 反而上升了！\\n这是因为 grammar 将 OOV relations 强制映射到合法关系名，暴露了 latent DR violations。\\n审稿人攻击：\\\"Grammar constraint reveals that the TRUE DR rate is 25%, not 15.5%. \\nThe unconstrained baseline's seemingly lower DR is an artifact of unrecognized relations \\nbeing excluded from DR calculation. The actual problem is LARGER than reported.\\\"\\n更关键的是：grammar-only ALREADY achieves the E-F1 gain（+1.7pp）——semantic 层\\n对 F1 没有额外贡献，它只贡献 DR reduction + CF introduction。\\n\"\n180\t  },\n181\t  {\n182\t    \"name\": \"DocRED semantic-only\",\n183\t    \"description\": \"DocRED 仅 semantic 层约束\",\n184\t    \"results\": {\n185\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.118,\n186\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.045,\n187\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.298,\n188\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.015,\n189\t      \"entity_f1\": 56.2,\n190\t      \"relation_f1\": 7.0\n191\t    },\n192\t    \"tables\": [],\n193\t    \"figures\": [],\n194\t    \"analysis\": \"\\\"Enabling dependency\\\" 在 worst 档被读为 \\\"tight coupling\\\" 和 \\\"design limitation\\\"——\\n方法无法 gracefully 在只有一层时工作，削弱了 \\\"composable framework\\\" 的 novelty claim。\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only 将 DR 从 15.5%→11.8%（↓24%），但无法处理 RV/ET，且 E-F1 下降 0.6pp\\n（因为 OOV relations 仍在，且 semantic masking 偶尔强制次优 token）。\\nCF 升至 1.5%（15×）。审稿人：\\\"Without grammar, the semantic layer achieves only \\nmodest DR reduction (24%) while degrading F1. It cannot function independently — \\nthis is not a composable architecture, it's a tightly-coupled system where one layer \\nis a prerequisite for the other.\\\"\\n\"\n195\t  },\n196\t  {\n197\t    \"name\": \"DocRED full S1\",\n198\t    \"description\": \"DocRED Grammar+Semantic 双层 S1 完整约束\",\n199\t    \"results\": {\n200\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.135,\n201\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n202\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n203\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.038,\n204\t      \"entity_f1\": 57.8,\n205\t      \"relation_f1\": 7.5,\n206\t      \"fallback_rate\": 0.58\n207\t    },\n208\t    \"tables\": [\n209\t      \"Table 5: SciERC DR↓80% vs DocRED DR↓13% — method effectiveness inversely correlated with schema complexity\"\n210\t    ],\n211\t    \"figures\": [],\n212\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED 结果是 worst 档最致命的实验：方法在大 ontology 上近乎失败。\\n结合 \\\"post-hoc is simpler and higher F1\\\" 论点，审稿人可以论证 OntoCoDec 仅适用于\\ntoy-scale ontology（SciERC 7 relations），不具备实际研究价值。\\nFallback rate 58% 揭示：方法在多数时刻降级为 grammar-only——\\\"the semantic layer \\nis more often disabled than active.\\\"\\n\\n\\nDR 从 15.5%→13.5%（仅↓13%）——这是 worst 档的 killer result。DocRED 上方法几乎\\n不工作。原因：constraint tightness 极高导致 semantic mask 频繁与 grammar mask 冲突，\\nfallback rate 达 58%，超过半数 token 位置只有 grammar-only 在生效。\\nCF=3.8%（从 0.1% 升 38×），E-F1 从 56.8 升到 57.8（+1.0pp，全部来自 grammar 层消除 OOV），\\nR-F1 从 7.2 升到 7.5（+0.3pp，来自 grammar）。\\n审稿人核心攻击：\\n\\\"On DocRED, the method reduces DR by only 2pp (15.5%→13.5%) — a 13% relative reduction \\ncompared to the claimed 94% on SciERC. The method's effectiveness is HIGHLY \\ndataset-dependent and essentially fails on the larger, more realistic dataset.\\\"\\n\"\n213\t  },\n214\t  {\n215\t    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC unconstrained\",\n216\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B 在 SciERC 上的 unconstrained baseline\",\n217\t    \"results\": {\n218\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.098,\n219\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.002,\n220\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.008,\n221\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.225,\n222\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.024,\n223\t      \"total_relations\": 1180\n224\t    },\n225\t    \"tables\": [],\n226\t    \"figures\": [],\n227\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model 的 baseline 差异被审稿人解读为 \\\"problem severity is model-specific\\\"——\\n如果用更强的 model，violation rate 自然下降，不需要 constrained decoding。\\n低 F1 进一步削弱结果的 credibility。\\n\\n\\nLlama baseline DR=9.8%——比 Qwen 的 12.8% 显著更低。审稿人论证：\\n\\\"Different models have different baseline violation rates (9.8% vs 12.8%). \\nA stronger model or better prompting could reduce violations without any \\nconstrained decoding. The problem magnitude is model-dependent, not fundamental.\\\"\\n更关键：Llama R-F1 仅 2.4%（比 Qwen 的 7.6% 低很多），表明 Llama 在 SciERC 上\\n几乎不能提取关系——在这种 near-random 输出上做 constraint enforcement 无意义。\\n\"\n228\t  },\n229\t  {\n230\t    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC full S1\",\n231\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B 在 SciERC 上的 full constrained decoding\",\n232\t    \"results\": {\n233\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.018,\n234\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n235\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0,\n236\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.095,\n237\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.218,\n238\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.021,\n239\t      \"parse_failures\": 8\n240\t    },\n241\t    \"tables\": [],\n242\t    \"figures\": [],\n243\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama 结果看似 \\\"consistent\\\"（DR↓82% 与 Qwen ↓80% 接近），但 absolute F1 太低\\n使得结果没有实际意义。审稿人会说 \\\"generalization to Llama just confirms the method \\nis equally ineffective across models — consistently trading DR for CF on garbage outputs.\\\"\\n\\n\\nDR 从 9.8%→1.8%（↓82%）——比 SciERC/Qwen 的 ↓80% 接近，看似一致。\\n但 CF=9.5%（比 Qwen 的 14.2% 低但仍极高），R-F1 下降 0.3pp（2.4%→2.1%）。\\n审稿人攻击：\\\"On Llama, the method reduces DR from a moderate 9.8% to 1.8%, \\nwhile introducing 9.5% CF and degrading an already-terrible F1. For a model \\nwith only 2.4% relation F1, constraint enforcement is clearly pointless — \\nyou're polishing type-valid garbage.\\\"\\nDR residual 1.8%（非 near-complete）+ CF 9.5% 的 trade-off 被视为 net negative。\\n\"\n244\t  },\n245\t  {\n246\t    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED unconstrained\",\n247\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B 在 DocRED 上的 unconstrained baseline\",\n248\t    \"results\": {\n249\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.228,\n250\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.165,\n251\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.002,\n252\t      \"entity_f1\": 54.5,\n253\t      \"relation_f1\": 5.5,\n254\t      \"parse_failures\": 75,\n255\t      \"total_triples\": 15800\n256\t    },\n257\t    \"tables\": [],\n258\t    \"figures\": [],\n259\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model DR 差异（15.5% vs 22.8%）在 worst 档不是 \\\"interesting finding\\\"，\\n而是 \\\"measurement instability\\\"——同一 ontology 的 violation landscape 因模型而异，\\n削弱了 violation landscape 作为 dataset/ontology 固有属性的 framing。\\n\\n\\nLlama DocRED DR=22.8%——高于 Qwen 的 15.5%，与 \\\"RV baseline 不同导致 DR 不同\\\" 的\\nactual finding 类似。但在 worst 档，审稿人会说：\\n\\\"Violation rates vary by 7.3pp across models on the same dataset (15.5% vs 22.8%).\\nThis model-dependence undermines any universal characterization of the 'violation landscape.'\\nThe paper cannot claim a dataset-level property when the measurement changes 50% \\ndepending on which model you use.\\\"\\nParse failures=75/998（7.5%）进一步削弱 claim 的 robustness。\\n\"\n260\t  },\n261\t  {\n262\t    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED full S1\",\n263\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B 在 DocRED 上的 full constrained decoding\",\n264\t    \"results\": {\n265\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.092,\n266\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n267\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0,\n268\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.155,\n269\t      \"entity_f1\": 53.2,\n270\t      \"relation_f1\": 5.1,\n271\t      \"parse_failures\": 105,\n272\t      \"fallback_rate\": 0.63\n273\t    },\n274\t    \"tables\": [\n275\t      \"Table 6: Cross-model × cross-dataset effectiveness matrix showing high variance (↓13% to ↓82%)\"\n276\t    ],\n277\t    \"figures\": [],\n278\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama DocRED 是 worst 档位的 \\\"smoking gun\\\"：DR↓60% 但 CF↑155×，F1↓，parse failures↑。\\n审稿人可以合法地说 \\\"the method is harmful on realistic-scale ontologies\\\"。\\n与 SciERC 的 good results 对比，构建 \\\"method only works on toy problems\\\" 叙事。\\n\\n\\nDR 从 22.8%→9.2%（↓60%）——比 Qwen DocRED 的 ↓13% 好，但远不如 SciERC 的 ↓80-82%。\\nCF=15.5%（极高！），E-F1 下降 1.3pp，R-F1 下降 0.4pp。Parse failures 从 75 升到 105。\\nFallback rate 63% 意味着 semantic layer 大部分时间被 bypass。\\n审稿人核心论点：\\n\\\"On DocRED with Llama, the method's DR reduction is 60% but introduces a CF rate \\nof 15.5% — meaning one in six entity type assignments is internally inconsistent. \\nCombined with F1 degradation and increased parse failures, the method is clearly \\nharmful on this dataset-model combination.\\\"\\nDR 残余 9.2% 也远高于 \\\"near-complete elimination\\\" 的任何合理定义。\\n\"\n279\t  },\n280\t  {\n281\t    \"name\": \"S2 pilot (50 docs)\",\n282\t    \"description\": \"S2 two-pass 小规模验证实验\",\n283\t    \"results\": {\n284\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.04,\n285\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.065,\n286\t      \"samples\": 50,\n287\t      \"predicted_relations\": 130\n288\t    },\n289\t    \"tables\": [],\n290\t    \"figures\": [],\n291\t    \"analysis\": \"Pilot 结果在论文中不应出现（已经有 full run），但在 supplementary material 中\\n如果被发现 pilot ≠ full run，会被解读为 \\\"selective reporting\\\"。\\n\\n\\nPilot 规模太小不能得出任何结论。Worst 档审稿人不会攻击 pilot 本身，\\n而是攻击 \\\"为什么在 pilot 明显表现不佳（R-F1 6.5% < S1 的 7.1%）的情况下\\n仍然跑了 full S2 experiment？这暗示作者在 p-hacking 寻找有利结果。\\\"\\n\"\n292\t  },\n293\t  {\n294\t    \"name\": \"Post-hoc filtering baseline\",\n295\t    \"description\": \"简单的事后过滤 baseline——移除所有 type-violating triples\",\n296\t    \"results\": {\n297\t      \"scierc_f1_before\": 7.6,\n298\t      \"scierc_f1_posthoc\": 8.9,\n299\t      \"scierc_f1_constrained\": 7.1,\n300\t      \"scierc_rejection_rate\": 0.145,\n301\t      \"scierc_dr_after\": 0,\n302\t      \"docred_f1_before\": 7.2,\n303\t      \"docred_f1_posthoc\": 10.2,\n304\t      \"docred_f1_constrained\": 7.5,\n305\t      \"docred_rejection_rate\": 0.52,\n306\t      \"docred_dr_after\": 0,\n307\t      \"docred_et_residual\": 0.025\n308\t    },\n309\t    \"tables\": [\n310\t      \"Table 7: Post-hoc vs Constrained — post-hoc dominates on F1 AND DR simultaneously\"\n311\t    ],\n312\t    \"figures\": [],\n313\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档位审稿人最强的 technical argument：\\\"A trivial baseline that the authors \\nthemselves implemented proves their complex method is unnecessary. The simpler approach \\nachieves better results on every metric the paper reports. This is a fatal flaw.\\\"\\n论文的 recall/coverage defense 在 7% F1 regime 下完全无力——who cares about recall \\nof type-valid triples when 93% of all triples are wrong anyway?\\n\\n\\nPost-hoc filtering 在两个数据集上都实现 higher F1：\\n- SciERC: post-hoc 8.9% vs constrained 7.1%（+1.8pp）\\n- DocRED: post-hoc 10.2% vs constrained 7.5%（+2.7pp）\\n且 post-hoc DR=0%（完美消除，无残余），而 constrained 仍有 2-13.5% 残余 DR。\\n审稿人的 killer argument：\\n\\\"Post-hoc filtering achieves BOTH better F1 (+1.8 to +2.7pp) AND better DR (0% vs 2-14%)\\nthan constrained decoding. It is simpler (one line of code), faster (no runtime overhead), \\nand more effective. The only advantage of constrained decoding — recall preservation — \\nis marginal (0.3-0.5pp) and unlikely to matter at these absolute F1 levels.\\\"\\nDocRED rejection rate 52% 本应是 post-hoc 的弱点，但在 F1-focused 审稿人眼中：\\n\\\"Rejecting 52% of near-random outputs (R-F1=7.2%) is a feature, not a bug.\\\"\\n\"\n314\t  },\n315\t  {\n316\t    \"name\": \"Bootstrap CI (10000 iterations)\",\n317\t    \"description\": \"Bootstrap 置信区间统计检验——确认 F1 差异显著性\",\n318\t    \"results\": {\n319\t      \"scierc_r_f1_delta\": -0.52,\n320\t      \"scierc_r_f1_p_value\": 0.02,\n321\t      \"scierc_r_f1_ci\": [\n322\t        -0.95,\n323\t        -0.08\n324\t      ],\n325\t      \"docred_r_f1_delta\": 0.28,\n326\t      \"docred_r_f1_p_value\": 0.08,\n327\t      \"docred_r_f1_ci\": [\n328\t        -0.04,\n329\t        0.61\n330\t      ],\n331\t      \"docred_e_f1_delta\": 0.95,\n332\t      \"docred_e_f1_p_value\": 0.002\n333\t    },\n334\t    \"tables\": [\n335\t      \"Table 8: Bootstrap results — significant F1 degradation on SciERC, non-significant on DocRED\"\n336\t    ],\n337\t    \"figures\": [],\n338\t    \"analysis\": \"统计检验在 worst 档反而成为武器：它 PROVES F1 degradation。\\n\\\"The paper honestly reports that their method significantly hurts performance on one \\ndataset and shows no significant improvement on the other. Combined with post-hoc's \\nsuperior F1, there is no quality argument for constrained decoding.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI 确认：\\n- SciERC R-F1 下降 0.52pp 且 statistically significant（p=0.02, CI 不跨 0）\\n- DocRED R-F1 上升 0.28pp 但 NOT significant（p=0.08, CI 跨 0）\\n审稿人攻击：\\n\\\"The authors' own statistical test shows constrained decoding SIGNIFICANTLY degrades \\nrelation F1 on SciERC (p=0.02). On DocRED, the improvement is not significant (p=0.08).\\nThere is NO dataset where the method improves F1 at conventional significance levels, \\nbut there IS one where it significantly hurts.\\\"\\nDocRED E-F1 的显著提升（+0.95pp, p=0.002）被归因于 grammar 层消除 OOV——\\n\\\"This gain comes from grammar (off-the-shelf XGrammar), not from the novel semantic layer.\\\"\\n\"\n339\t  },\n340\t  {\n341\t    \"name\": \"DocRED schema compilation (Phase 0 R2)\",\n342\t    \"description\": \"DocRED schema-informed prompt 重跑（被 P004 supersede）\",\n343\t    \"results\": {\n344\t      \"status\": \"killed\"\n345\t    },\n346\t    \"tables\": [],\n347\t    \"figures\": [],\n348\t    \"analysis\": \"无实质影响，但应确保 paper 中不引用此实验的任何中间结果。\\n\\n实验被终止，无结果。在 worst 档，审稿人不会关注 killed experiments，\\n但如果在 supplementary 中被发现，可能被解读为 \\\"the authors killed experiments \\nthat produced unfavorable results\\\" — selective reporting suspicion。\\n\"\n349\t  }\n350\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7520a298-8466-4fc2-9ef4-158ddc28c35f","uuid":"edca579c-e255-4405-8d5e-96cbe4e56180","timestamp":"2026-05-16T18:00:26.085Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T173022/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Zero-shot Qwen3-8B 在 SciERC 上的 ontology constraint violation baseline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 1680,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.128,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.005,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.018,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.295,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.076,\n      \"per_relation_dr_variance\": 0.008,\n      \"max_per_relation_dr\": 0.31,\n      \"min_per_relation_dr\": 0.04\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: Per-relation DR distribution — relatively flat, max/min ratio ~8× (not 55× as needed for tightness argument)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"审稿人攻击线：\\\"The violation rates are moderate and relatively uniform — this is \\nsimply what happens when you ask an LLM to generate structured output without fine-tuning.\\nThe 'violation landscape' contribution reduces to measuring a known phenomenon.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档位下，DR 约 12.8%——仍属 non-trivial 但低于 15% 的 \\\"impressive\\\" 门槛。\\n关键问题：per-relation DR variance 较低（σ²=0.008），violations 分布相对均匀，\\n削弱了 \\\"constraint tightness drives concentration\\\" 的核心 insight。\\n审稿人会说：\\\"12.8% violation rate across 7 relations is expected for any structured \\ngeneration task — this is not a surprising finding worthy of a dedicated landscape study.\\\"\\n最高单关系 DR 仅 31%（非 42%），不够极端来论证 per-relation guarantee 的必要性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Schema-informed prompt 对 SciERC violations 的消除效果\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.041,\n      \"total_triples\": 1640,\n      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction\": -0.68,\n      \"per_relation_evaluate_for_delta\": -0.02,\n      \"per_relation_feature_of_delta\": -0.24,\n      \"per_relation_all_improved\": true,\n      \"mcnemar_significant\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"如果 prompt 足够好且无 regression，整个 \\\"prompt insufficiency\\\" claim 被削弱。\\n审稿人会追问：\\\"Why not iterate on prompt engineering (few-shot, chain-of-thought) \\nbefore building a complex decoding system?\\\" OntoCoDec 变成 over-engineering 的例证。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档：schema-informed prompt 将 DR 从 12.8% 降到 4.1%（↓68%），且所有关系类型均有改善\\n（Evaluate-for 也下降 2pp 而非实际的 +5.8pp regression）。审稿人论证：\\n\\\"A well-crafted prompt already achieves 68% reduction with zero engineering effort. \\nThe remaining 4.1% is close to noise level for zero-shot extraction. The cost-benefit \\nof building a compiler + runtime constraint system for the last 4pp is questionable.\\\"\\n没有 per-relation regression = 丢失了 \\\"prompt unreliable at per-relation level\\\" 这个关键论据。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED 96-relation ontology 的 zero-shot violation baseline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 16200,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.155,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.068,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.295,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.958\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: Cross-dataset comparison — DR rates within 3pp, undermining urgency narrative\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RV=29.5% 被审稿人视为 grammar 层的 \\\"free lunch\\\"——单层 CFG constraint 就能消除的 trivial violation，\\n不需要复杂的 semantic layer。\\\"Most of the violations (29.5% RV + 6.8% ET = 36.3%) are \\ntrivially fixable by grammar alone; only 15.5% require semantic reasoning.\\\"\\n\\n\\nDR=15.5% 与 SciERC 12.8% 接近（比值 1.2×）——审稿人论证：\\n\\\"Violation rates are comparable across a 7-relation and 96-relation ontology (15.5% vs 12.8%). \\nThis directly contradicts any claim about ontology complexity driving violations — \\nthe rates are essentially the same regardless of schema size.\\\"\\n这个数据点本应支持 \\\"tightness not size\\\" 的 insight，但在 worst 档位下被反过来读：\\n既然 rate 不随 size 变化，问题规模本身就是 bounded（不像论文暗示的那样严峻）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Schema-informed prompt 在 DocRED 上的效果\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.098,\n      \"dr_reduction_vs_minimal\": -0.37,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.19\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"审稿人构建 \\\"diminishing returns\\\" 叙事：Prompt ↓37% (free) → FT ↓95% (standard) → \\nConstrained decoding covers the last 2% at the cost of CF↑10× and latency overhead.\\n\\\"The method lives in a narrow utility window that disappears with standard fine-tuning.\\\"\\n\\n\\nDR 降到 9.8%（↓37%）——比 SciERC 的 ↓68% 弱，但审稿人不关注这个 gap：\\n\\\"Even with a simple schema-informed prompt, DR drops to under 10%. Combined with \\nthe fact that fine-tuning reduces DR to <2%, the remaining window where constrained \\ndecoding adds value is extremely narrow (the 2-10% gap that prompt can't close but \\nFT can).\\\" 这直接喂 \\\"FT makes the method unnecessary\\\" 攻击线。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"SciERC Phase 2 unconstrained 重跑（checker v2 对齐）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.128,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.018,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.005,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.295,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.076,\n      \"total_triples\": 1680\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"低 F1 baseline 是 C8 攻击面的核心弹药。Worst 档审稿人不会接受 \\\"F1 is control variable\\\"\\n的论证——他们会说 \\\"if the base extraction is this poor, constraint enforcement \\nis premature optimization on garbage.\\\"\\n\\n\\n与 P001 一致（同一模型同一数据集），作为 Phase 2 ablation 的对照基线。\\nWorst 档位下 baseline F1 已经很低（R-F1 7.6%），审稿人会质疑：\\n\\\"Evaluating constraint methods on a setting with 7.6% relation F1 is meaningless — \\nthe model barely extracts anything correctly. Any constraint enforcement on \\nnear-random outputs is academic exercise, not useful research.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC grammar-only\",\n    \"description\": \"仅 grammar 层（CFG）对 SciERC 的约束效果\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.125,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.294,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.075\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Grammar 层的效果完全可预期且 trivial——这是 worst 档审稿人最强的 novelty 攻击弹药。\\n\\\"Layer 1 is off-the-shelf XGrammar. Layer 2 is a type checker. The paper's contribution \\nis connecting them with bitwise AND — this is systems integration, not research.\\\"\\n\\n\\nGrammar 层消除 ET/RV（trivial CFG-expressible constraints），但 DR 仅从 12.8%→12.5%\\n（↓2.3%，negligible）。F1 微降 0.1pp。审稿人的读法：\\n\\\"The grammar layer does exactly what XGrammar was designed to do — enforce vocabulary \\nconstraints. This is a direct application of existing technology (XGrammar, Zheng et al. 2024) \\nwith zero methodological novelty. The authors simply configured XGrammar for their JSON schema.\\\"\\n这直接喂 \\\"engineering contribution\\\" 的 novelty 攻击。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC semantic-only\",\n    \"description\": \"仅 semantic 层（logit masking）对 SciERC 的约束效果\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.088,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.005,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.018,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.035,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.292,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.073\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Semantic-only 的 CF 引入是最致命的数据点：它证明 semantic 层 IS the source of CF，\\n且没有 grammar 层时效果很差。审稿人会说 \\\"the semantic layer is both the cause of \\nthe new problem (CF) and insufficient to solve the original problem (DR) without grammar.\\\"\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only 将 DR 从 12.8%→8.8%（↓31%），但引入 CF=3.5%（从 0.1% 暴涨 35×）。\\nF1 下降 0.3pp。审稿人攻击：\\\"The semantic layer alone achieves only 31% DR reduction \\nwhile introducing 35× more cross-field inconsistencies. This is a net negative — \\nthe method creates more problems than it solves.\\\"\\n且 ET/RV 无法处理（因为没有 grammar 层），暴露 enabling dependency 但被读为 \\\"单层无法独立工作 = 设计耦合\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"Grammar+Semantic 双层 single-pass decoding 对 SciERC 的完整效果\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.025,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.142,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.289,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.071,\n      \"fallback_rate\": 0.41\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3: Violation trade-off — DR↓10.3pp vs CF↑14.1pp, net violation increase\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档位的核心数据：方法引入的 CF 大于它消除的 DR。\\ntotal_violation_before = 12.8% + 1.8% + 0.5% + 0.1% = 15.2%\\ntotal_violation_after = 2.5% + 0% + 0% + 14.2% = 16.7%\\n审稿人可以合法地声称 \\\"the method makes things worse on aggregate.\\\"\\n即使论证 DR > CF in severity，这个 framing 对 EMNLP reviewer 极具说服力。\\n\\n\\nDR 从 12.8%→2.5%（↓80%），但 CF 从 0.1%→14.2%（↑142×）。\\nR-F1 下降 0.5pp（p=0.03, statistically significant）。\\n审稿人的核心攻击：\\n\\\"The method reduces DR by 10.3pp but introduces CF at 14.2pp — a net INCREASE \\nin total violation load. The authors are trading known, measurable violations \\n(DR) for harder-to-detect inconsistencies (CF). This is not improvement, \\nit's problem displacement.\\\"\\nFallback rate 41% 意味着近半数 token 位置 semantic mask 失效——方法在很多时刻\\n实质上只有 grammar-only 在工作。DR 残余 2.5%（非 near-complete）进一步削弱 claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC full S2 (ablation)\",\n    \"description\": \"Two-pass S2 策略作为 CF mitigation 的尝试\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.028,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.128,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.285,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.068,\n      \"total_entities\": 2180\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"S2 在所有指标上都不如 S1 或仅 marginal 改善——审稿人会说 \\\"the authors tried to fix CF \\nwith a two-pass approach and failed. This confirms CF is a fundamental limitation \\nof the approach, not an engineering issue that can be resolved.\\\"\\n\\n\\nS2 DR=2.8%（比 S1 的 2.5% 更差），CF=12.8%（比 S1 的 14.2% 稍好但仍然极高）。\\nR-F1 6.8%（比 S1 的 7.1% 更差 0.3pp）。Entity 数量从 2474 降到 2180（↓12%）——\\nS2 pass-1 的 entity extraction 更保守但不更准确。\\n审稿人：\\\"The two-pass variant slightly reduces CF (14.2%→12.8%) but at the cost of \\nworse F1 and higher DR. The proposed architectural solution to CF does not work.\\\"\\nS2 无法作为 CF mitigation 的证据，也无法作为 interesting architectural contribution。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED Phase 2 unconstrained（checker v2, all_set F1）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.155,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.295,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.068,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"entity_f1\": 56.8,\n      \"relation_f1\": 7.2,\n      \"total_triples\": 17100,\n      \"unrecognized_relations\": 5050\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"High RV% 在 worst 档被解读为 \\\"大部分 contribution 来自 off-the-shelf grammar constraint\\\"，\\n留给 semantic 层的独有贡献空间只有 15.5pp DR。\\n\\n\\nDocRED baseline 的 RV=29.5% 和 ET=6.8% 是 grammar 层的 \\\"easy wins\\\"——\\n审稿人会计算：\\\"36.3% of violations are trivially fixable by vocabulary constraint \\n(XGrammar direct application), only 15.5% require the novel semantic layer.\\\"\\nE-F1=56.8% 比 SciERC 高很多，因为 DocRED entity recognition 相对简单\\n（named entities vs scientific terms）。R-F1=7.2% 仍然很低。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED grammar-only\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED 仅 grammar 层约束\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.25,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"entity_f1\": 58.5,\n      \"relation_f1\": 7.9\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: Grammar-only achieves ALL of the F1 improvement; semantic layer contributes zero F1 gain\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"\\\"Grammar layer = all F1 gain. Semantic layer = DR↓ + CF↑ + 0 F1 impact.\\\" \\n这是 worst 档审稿人最简洁有力的论证——semantic 层的 contribution 是 DR→CF 的 trade-off，\\n而非 F1 improvement。整个 semantic 层可以被 post-hoc filter 替代且更简单。\\n\\n\\nGrammar-only 消除 RV 和 ET（36.3pp violations gone），E-F1 提升 1.7pp（从 OOV relation \\n不再作为 FP 计入），R-F1 提升 0.7pp。DR 从 15.5%→25.0%——注意 DR 反而上升了！\\n这是因为 grammar 将 OOV relations 强制映射到合法关系名，暴露了 latent DR violations。\\n审稿人攻击：\\\"Grammar constraint reveals that the TRUE DR rate is 25%, not 15.5%. \\nThe unconstrained baseline's seemingly lower DR is an artifact of unrecognized relations \\nbeing excluded from DR calculation. The actual problem is LARGER than reported.\\\"\\n更关键的是：grammar-only ALREADY achieves the E-F1 gain（+1.7pp）——semantic 层\\n对 F1 没有额外贡献，它只贡献 DR reduction + CF introduction。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED semantic-only\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED 仅 semantic 层约束\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.118,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.045,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.298,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.015,\n      \"entity_f1\": 56.2,\n      \"relation_f1\": 7.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"\\\"Enabling dependency\\\" 在 worst 档被读为 \\\"tight coupling\\\" 和 \\\"design limitation\\\"——\\n方法无法 gracefully 在只有一层时工作，削弱了 \\\"composable framework\\\" 的 novelty claim。\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only 将 DR 从 15.5%→11.8%（↓24%），但无法处理 RV/ET，且 E-F1 下降 0.6pp\\n（因为 OOV relations 仍在，且 semantic masking 偶尔强制次优 token）。\\nCF 升至 1.5%（15×）。审稿人：\\\"Without grammar, the semantic layer achieves only \\nmodest DR reduction (24%) while degrading F1. It cannot function independently — \\nthis is not a composable architecture, it's a tightly-coupled system where one layer \\nis a prerequisite for the other.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED Grammar+Semantic 双层 S1 完整约束\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.135,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.038,\n      \"entity_f1\": 57.8,\n      \"relation_f1\": 7.5,\n      \"fallback_rate\": 0.58\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: SciERC DR↓80% vs DocRED DR↓13% — method effectiveness inversely correlated with schema complexity\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED 结果是 worst 档最致命的实验：方法在大 ontology 上近乎失败。\\n结合 \\\"post-hoc is simpler and higher F1\\\" 论点，审稿人可以论证 OntoCoDec 仅适用于\\ntoy-scale ontology（SciERC 7 relations），不具备实际研究价值。\\nFallback rate 58% 揭示：方法在多数时刻降级为 grammar-only——\\\"the semantic layer \\nis more often disabled than active.\\\"\\n\\n\\nDR 从 15.5%→13.5%（仅↓13%）——这是 worst 档的 killer result。DocRED 上方法几乎\\n不工作。原因：constraint tightness 极高导致 semantic mask 频繁与 grammar mask 冲突，\\nfallback rate 达 58%，超过半数 token 位置只有 grammar-only 在生效。\\nCF=3.8%（从 0.1% 升 38×），E-F1 从 56.8 升到 57.8（+1.0pp，全部来自 grammar 层消除 OOV），\\nR-F1 从 7.2 升到 7.5（+0.3pp，来自 grammar）。\\n审稿人核心攻击：\\n\\\"On DocRED, the method reduces DR by only 2pp (15.5%→13.5%) — a 13% relative reduction \\ncompared to the claimed 94% on SciERC. The method's effectiveness is HIGHLY \\ndataset-dependent and essentially fails on the larger, more realistic dataset.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC unconstrained\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B 在 SciERC 上的 unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.098,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.002,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.008,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.225,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.024,\n      \"total_relations\": 1180\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model 的 baseline 差异被审稿人解读为 \\\"problem severity is model-specific\\\"——\\n如果用更强的 model，violation rate 自然下降，不需要 constrained decoding。\\n低 F1 进一步削弱结果的 credibility。\\n\\n\\nLlama baseline DR=9.8%——比 Qwen 的 12.8% 显著更低。审稿人论证：\\n\\\"Different models have different baseline violation rates (9.8% vs 12.8%). \\nA stronger model or better prompting could reduce violations without any \\nconstrained decoding. The problem magnitude is model-dependent, not fundamental.\\\"\\n更关键：Llama R-F1 仅 2.4%（比 Qwen 的 7.6% 低很多），表明 Llama 在 SciERC 上\\n几乎不能提取关系——在这种 near-random 输出上做 constraint enforcement 无意义。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B 在 SciERC 上的 full constrained decoding\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.018,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.095,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.218,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.021,\n      \"parse_failures\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama 结果看似 \\\"consistent\\\"（DR↓82% 与 Qwen ↓80% 接近），但 absolute F1 太低\\n使得结果没有实际意义。审稿人会说 \\\"generalization to Llama just confirms the method \\nis equally ineffective across models — consistently trading DR for CF on garbage outputs.\\\"\\n\\n\\nDR 从 9.8%→1.8%（↓82%）——比 SciERC/Qwen 的 ↓80% 接近，看似一致。\\n但 CF=9.5%（比 Qwen 的 14.2% 低但仍极高），R-F1 下降 0.3pp（2.4%→2.1%）。\\n审稿人攻击：\\\"On Llama, the method reduces DR from a moderate 9.8% to 1.8%, \\nwhile introducing 9.5% CF and degrading an already-terrible F1. For a model \\nwith only 2.4% relation F1, constraint enforcement is clearly pointless — \\nyou're polishing type-valid garbage.\\\"\\nDR residual 1.8%（非 near-complete）+ CF 9.5% 的 trade-off 被视为 net negative。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED unconstrained\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B 在 DocRED 上的 unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.228,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.165,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.002,\n      \"entity_f1\": 54.5,\n      \"relation_f1\": 5.5,\n      \"parse_failures\": 75,\n      \"total_triples\": 15800\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model DR 差异（15.5% vs 22.8%）在 worst 档不是 \\\"interesting finding\\\"，\\n而是 \\\"measurement instability\\\"——同一 ontology 的 violation landscape 因模型而异，\\n削弱了 violation landscape 作为 dataset/ontology 固有属性的 framing。\\n\\n\\nLlama DocRED DR=22.8%——高于 Qwen 的 15.5%，与 \\\"RV baseline 不同导致 DR 不同\\\" 的\\nactual finding 类似。但在 worst 档，审稿人会说：\\n\\\"Violation rates vary by 7.3pp across models on the same dataset (15.5% vs 22.8%).\\nThis model-dependence undermines any universal characterization of the 'violation landscape.'\\nThe paper cannot claim a dataset-level property when the measurement changes 50% \\ndepending on which model you use.\\\"\\nParse failures=75/998（7.5%）进一步削弱 claim 的 robustness。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B 在 DocRED 上的 full constrained decoding\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.092,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.155,\n      \"entity_f1\": 53.2,\n      \"relation_f1\": 5.1,\n      \"parse_failures\": 105,\n      \"fallback_rate\": 0.63\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6: Cross-model × cross-dataset effectiveness matrix showing high variance (↓13% to ↓82%)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama DocRED 是 worst 档位的 \\\"smoking gun\\\"：DR↓60% 但 CF↑155×，F1↓，parse failures↑。\\n审稿人可以合法地说 \\\"the method is harmful on realistic-scale ontologies\\\"。\\n与 SciERC 的 good results 对比，构建 \\\"method only works on toy problems\\\" 叙事。\\n\\n\\nDR 从 22.8%→9.2%（↓60%）——比 Qwen DocRED 的 ↓13% 好，但远不如 SciERC 的 ↓80-82%。\\nCF=15.5%（极高！），E-F1 下降 1.3pp，R-F1 下降 0.4pp。Parse failures 从 75 升到 105。\\nFallback rate 63% 意味着 semantic layer 大部分时间被 bypass。\\n审稿人核心论点：\\n\\\"On DocRED with Llama, the method's DR reduction is 60% but introduces a CF rate \\nof 15.5% — meaning one in six entity type assignments is internally inconsistent. \\nCombined with F1 degradation and increased parse failures, the method is clearly \\nharmful on this dataset-model combination.\\\"\\nDR 残余 9.2% 也远高于 \\\"near-complete elimination\\\" 的任何合理定义。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"S2 pilot (50 docs)\",\n    \"description\": \"S2 two-pass 小规模验证实验\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.04,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.065,\n      \"samples\": 50,\n      \"predicted_relations\": 130\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Pilot 结果在论文中不应出现（已经有 full run），但在 supplementary material 中\\n如果被发现 pilot ≠ full run，会被解读为 \\\"selective reporting\\\"。\\n\\n\\nPilot 规模太小不能得出任何结论。Worst 档审稿人不会攻击 pilot 本身，\\n而是攻击 \\\"为什么在 pilot 明显表现不佳（R-F1 6.5% < S1 的 7.1%）的情况下\\n仍然跑了 full S2 experiment？这暗示作者在 p-hacking 寻找有利结果。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Post-hoc filtering baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"简单的事后过滤 baseline——移除所有 type-violating triples\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"scierc_f1_before\": 7.6,\n      \"scierc_f1_posthoc\": 8.9,\n      \"scierc_f1_constrained\": 7.1,\n      \"scierc_rejection_rate\": 0.145,\n      \"scierc_dr_after\": 0,\n      \"docred_f1_before\": 7.2,\n      \"docred_f1_posthoc\": 10.2,\n      \"docred_f1_constrained\": 7.5,\n      \"docred_rejection_rate\": 0.52,\n      \"docred_dr_after\": 0,\n      \"docred_et_residual\": 0.025\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7: Post-hoc vs Constrained — post-hoc dominates on F1 AND DR simultaneously\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档位审稿人最强的 technical argument：\\\"A trivial baseline that the authors \\nthemselves implemented proves their complex method is unnecessary. The simpler approach \\nachieves better results on every metric the paper reports. This is a fatal flaw.\\\"\\n论文的 recall/coverage defense 在 7% F1 regime 下完全无力——who cares about recall \\nof type-valid triples when 93% of all triples are wrong anyway?\\n\\n\\nPost-hoc filtering 在两个数据集上都实现 higher F1：\\n- SciERC: post-hoc 8.9% vs constrained 7.1%（+1.8pp）\\n- DocRED: post-hoc 10.2% vs constrained 7.5%（+2.7pp）\\n且 post-hoc DR=0%（完美消除，无残余），而 constrained 仍有 2-13.5% 残余 DR。\\n审稿人的 killer argument：\\n\\\"Post-hoc filtering achieves BOTH better F1 (+1.8 to +2.7pp) AND better DR (0% vs 2-14%)\\nthan constrained decoding. It is simpler (one line of code), faster (no runtime overhead), \\nand more effective. The only advantage of constrained decoding — recall preservation — \\nis marginal (0.3-0.5pp) and unlikely to matter at these absolute F1 levels.\\\"\\nDocRED rejection rate 52% 本应是 post-hoc 的弱点，但在 F1-focused 审稿人眼中：\\n\\\"Rejecting 52% of near-random outputs (R-F1=7.2%) is a feature, not a bug.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bootstrap CI (10000 iterations)\",\n    \"description\": \"Bootstrap 置信区间统计检验——确认 F1 差异显著性\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"scierc_r_f1_delta\": -0.52,\n      \"scierc_r_f1_p_value\": 0.02,\n      \"scierc_r_f1_ci\": [\n        -0.95,\n        -0.08\n      ],\n      \"docred_r_f1_delta\": 0.28,\n      \"docred_r_f1_p_value\": 0.08,\n      \"docred_r_f1_ci\": [\n        -0.04,\n        0.61\n      ],\n      \"docred_e_f1_delta\": 0.95,\n      \"docred_e_f1_p_value\": 0.002\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 8: Bootstrap results — significant F1 degradation on SciERC, non-significant on DocRED\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"统计检验在 worst 档反而成为武器：它 PROVES F1 degradation。\\n\\\"The paper honestly reports that their method significantly hurts performance on one \\ndataset and shows no significant improvement on the other. Combined with post-hoc's \\nsuperior F1, there is no quality argument for constrained decoding.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI 确认：\\n- SciERC R-F1 下降 0.52pp 且 statistically significant（p=0.02, CI 不跨 0）\\n- DocRED R-F1 上升 0.28pp 但 NOT significant（p=0.08, CI 跨 0）\\n审稿人攻击：\\n\\\"The authors' own statistical test shows constrained decoding SIGNIFICANTLY degrades \\nrelation F1 on SciERC (p=0.02). On DocRED, the improvement is not significant (p=0.08).\\nThere is NO dataset where the method improves F1 at conventional significance levels, \\nbut there IS one where it significantly hurts.\\\"\\nDocRED E-F1 的显著提升（+0.95pp, p=0.002）被归因于 grammar 层消除 OOV——\\n\\\"This gain comes from grammar (off-the-shelf XGrammar), not from the novel semantic layer.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED schema compilation (Phase 0 R2)\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED schema-informed prompt 重跑（被 P004 supersede）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"killed\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"无实质影响，但应确保 paper 中不引用此实验的任何中间结果。\\n\\n实验被终止，无结果。在 worst 档，审稿人不会关注 killed experiments，\\n但如果在 supplementary 中被发现，可能被解读为 \\\"the authors killed experiments \\nthat produced unfavorable results\\\" — selective reporting suspicion。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":350,"startLine":1,"totalLines":350}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016LBGtn5WyvGqdrTRbDnf2j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the information I need. Let me understand the task:\n\n1. This is a \"worst\" tier dream paper - meaning I need to write a paper that presents the data from the perspective of the worst-case reviewer interpretation.\n2. The narrative guidance says to reframe as an analysis paper: \"When Does Constrained Decoding Help IE? A Decidability-Aware Analysis\"\n3. OntoCoDec is demoted to an analysis tool, CF becomes a key finding, FT regime marginal value becomes a finding\n\nLet me carefully extract the key data points from experiment_data.json:\n\n\nLooking at the SciERC results, I can see the violation patterns across different decoding strategies - the minimal prompt baseline shows substantial constraint violations across most categories, while schema-informed decoding dramatically reduces dependency relation violations by 68%, and the semantic-only approach interestingly introduces a spike in constraint violations at 3.5%.\n\nFor DocRED, the minimal prompt has even higher violation rates, particularly with relation violations at 29.5% and JSON parsing failures at 95.8%, though schema-informed decoding again provides significant improvements, cutting dependency relation violations down to 9.8%. Now I'm looking at the performance metrics across different models and datasets—comparing unconstrained approaches against the full constraint strategy, and seeing how post-hoc filtering and bootstrap confidence intervals affect the relation extraction F1 scores.\n\nFor the paper reframing, I'm positioning this as an analysis study that uses constrained decoding as a lens to understand when and why these techniques help or hurt information extraction, rather than treating the decoder itself as the main contribution. The confidence-frequency trade-off becomes a central finding that reveals somethin